# Line endings are a property of this repository, not of each contributor's
# core.autocrlf. Git stores every text file with LF; the working tree follows
# the platform.
#
# Without this, a file first committed with CRLF kept CRLF forever -- git does
# not renormalise a path whose index entry already has CRLF -- and became mixed
# as soon as an editor using LF added lines to it. Three files had ended up that
# way before this was introduced.
#
# Every tracked file here is text (.py, .cert PEM, .md, .txt, .in). If binary
# assets are ever committed, give them an explicit rule, e.g. `*.png binary`.
* text=auto
